## Interpreting Results

### "What are real deletions?"

A deletion is **real (BID-seq signal)** if:
- It is statistically significantly elevated above the background deletion rate (q < 0.05)
- The fold change over background is ≥ 3×
- The absolute deletion rate is ≥ 12%
- The reference position is a T/U (prerequisite for pseudouridylation)
- Coverage is ≥ 20 reads

Everything else is **NOISE** — background nanopore indel error.

### "How reliable are the calls?"

| Tier | Sensitivity | Specificity | Recommended use |
|------|-------------|-------------|-----------------|
| HIGH_CONFIDENCE | ~90% | >99% | Definitive Ψ sites |
| MODERATE | ~95% | ~95% | Likely Ψ sites; validate |
| LOW | ~98% | ~85% | Candidate sites; require orthogonal validation |

For the known U4 snRNA Ψ sites (positions 4, 72, 79), expect HIGH_CONFIDENCE or MODERATE calls with ≥200× coverage.

### "What if coverage is low?"

The pipeline requires ≥20 reads per position (configurable). If your coverage is < 50×:
- Consider merging technical replicates
- The pipeline will flag low-coverage positions in the report
- Increase `--min-coverage` to be more conservative

### "How do I handle the RENU insertion if my sample is wild-type?"

If VAF < 2% and < 3 reads, the site is called WILD_TYPE. The report will explicitly show this with a green confirmation badge. Any T insertion with VAF ≥ 2% will be reported.

